LOGBOOK.md:559:- DECISION: A10 became four assertions over a computed allowlist — completeness, containment, exclusion, channel hygiene — where the allowlist is authored keys ∪ always-injected ∪ (development-only if that channel). iOS spellings are recorded at **medium confidence** with `3dno4w` named as verifier, since no iOS bundle was built here; guessing them silently would have been the same class of error.
LOGBOOK.md:590:- ANOMALY: Round 2 described Ceremony C1 as one sitting, but no board element owned the sitting. The four grant-bearing tasks were ordered `apc34w` → {`3jloqy`, `dveo1o`}, so a `max_parallel = 1` scheduler produced **two** human stops with a full producer→reviewer cycle between them. Prose cannot batch a human interaction; only the DAG can. Recorded as ADR-028 and fixed by creating `TASK-260728-q5kjta`, the single up-front human-input node; `apc34w`, `3jloqy`, `dveo1o`, `ziprhs` are now unattended agent evidence tasks behind it, with their evidence obligations intact.
LOGBOOK.md:1206:- FINDING: swift-nio carries two additional 2026 medium HTTP-path advisories (GHSA-rj37-6j9x-74q6, GHSA-cq87-8r7h-962v) not enumerated in the audit; both are patched by the pinned `2.101.3`, so the security-baseline conclusion stands. E-SUPPLYCHAIN re-audit will re-enumerate.

